✔ a completed cleanup is terminal even when its numeric PGID later has unrelated members (2.785125ms)
✔ a closed launcher cannot signal a different group reusing its numeric PGID (1.176042ms)
✔ exit observed before pipe close already requires current group identity (0.840541ms)
✔ an orphan retaining the inherited ownership marker can still be cleaned (0.923542ms)
✔ identity must be rechecked before escalation after the first signal (0.873417ms)
✔ the ownership marker overrides a caller supplied marker without removing the caller environment (0.586959ms)
✔ an active owned launcher still follows the bounded normal termination path (0.776083ms)
✔ completed cleanup never inspects or signals a subsequently reused PGID (2.095875ms)
✔ closed launcher rejects an unrelated reused PGID on linux (0.870583ms)
✔ closed launcher rejects an unrelated reused PGID on darwin (0.511375ms)
✔ an inherited owner nonce permits orphan cleanup on linux (0.53225ms)
✔ an inherited owner nonce permits orphan cleanup on darwin (0.960125ms)
✔ an exited launcher with inherited open pipes already needs identity verification (0.652584ms)
✔ forced termination rechecks identity and never falls back to a stale PGID (0.543666ms)
✔ identity inspection errors do not expose captured environment or send a signal (0.410041ms)
✔ fresh launch inherits the default environment and adds its own marker (0.380834ms)
